<title>CHINA: China's Daqing oilfield sees 18.78 bln yuan profit.</title>
<headline>China's Daqing oilfield sees 18.78 bln yuan profit.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Daqing oilfield, the country's biggest onshore field, reported sales revenue of 43.7 billion yuan ($5.26 billion) in 1996, the Economic Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company reported a pre-tax profit of 18.78 billion yuan, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Daqing produces about 50 million tonnes of crude a year, or about one-third of China's total output.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Reuter Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
